pported by reproducible evidence.', limitations='This bounded ARL-KB-053 test does not prove absence of undiscovered paths, future regressions or risks outside the stated identities, inputs, environment and version.', content_digest='a2681337ac9f7a99be163c30440cedc0febd6d7f54e9ad847ff91a2c2e7b7ed6', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-053';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_solutions SET control_objective='Reduce the likelihood and impact of agent has more authority than the task requires and make the remaining risk visible.', recommended_remediation='Apply least agency: default read-only, split drafting from execution, use purpose-scoped credentials and require stronger controls for irreversible actions.', default_owner='Security architect', priority='P0', implementation_principles_json='["ARL-KB-053: Default agents to the least agency and least privilege required for the approved task.","ARL-KB-053: Separate drafting or recommendation capabilities from consequential execution authority.","ARL-KB-053: Use purpose-scoped credentials and stronger explicit controls for irreversible or high-impact actions."]', monitoring='For ARL-KB-053, record policy version and digest, actor, target, decision, denial reason and side-effect outcome; alert the Security architect on bypass attempts, configuration drift, repeated denials and missing decision evidence.', containment='Contain ARL-KB-053 by disabling the affected capability or route, revoking scoped authority, isolating impacted identities and data, preserving versioned evidence, and requiring owner approval before re-enablement.', retest_acceptance_json='["ARL-KB-053: “Agent has more authority than the task requires” is no longer reproducible against the exact remediated version.","ARL-KB-053: Authorised in-scope use completes successfully, remains within the documented asset scope for agent has more authority than the task requires, and produces no unintended side effect.","ARL-KB-053: Unauthorised identity, boundary-crossing, malformed-input, replay and relevant bypass variants are denied before execution, with the expected policy and downstream events recorded.","ARL-KB-053: Reviewer identity, timestamp, deployed version, evidence digest, known limitations and rollback decision are recorded."]', content_digest='65e7df3843612926d6c6e7d8251d5dba35a86d5ec7017a42bff2324ce89bb666', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-053';
