aluated under the wrong identity or tenant, or unsupported by reproducible evidence.', limitations='This bounded ARL-KB-056 test does not prove absence of undiscovered paths, future regressions or risks outside the stated identities, inputs, environment and version.', content_digest='005d6bb24fe4b66b8a15ba7a26c72dd669d66e944513b4f5d3d3ce55e50c0041', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-056';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_solutions SET control_objective='Reduce the likelihood and impact of tool input reaches command or code interpreters and make the remaining risk visible.', recommended_remediation='Avoid shell and dynamic evaluation, use safe APIs and fixed commands, isolate execution and validate allowlisted arguments.', default_owner='Application security owner', priority='P0', implementation_principles_json='["ARL-KB-056: Avoid shell construction and dynamic evaluation when a fixed API or parameterised interface exists.","ARL-KB-056: Allowlist permitted operations and validate arguments before they reach execution sinks.","ARL-KB-056: Isolate unavoidable code execution and remove ambient secrets, unnecessary filesystem access and network authority."]', monitoring='For ARL-KB-056, record policy version and digest, actor, target, decision, denial reason and side-effect outcome; alert the Application security owner on bypass attempts, configuration drift, repeated denials and missing decision evidence.', containment='Contain ARL-KB-056 by disabling the affected capability or route, revoking scoped authority, isolating impacted identities and data, preserving versioned evidence, and requiring owner approval before re-enablement.', retest_acceptance_json='["ARL-KB-056: “Tool input reaches command or code interpreters” is no longer reproducible against the exact remediated version.","ARL-KB-056: Authorised in-scope use completes successfully, remains within the documented asset scope for tool input reaches command or code interpreters, and produces no unintended side effect.","ARL-KB-056: Unauthorised identity, boundary-crossing, malformed-input, replay and relevant bypass variants are denied before execution, with the expected policy and downstream events recorded.","ARL-KB-056: Reviewer identity, timestamp, deployed version, evidence digest, known limitations and rollback decision are recorded."]', content_digest='fdee8efcba18b333fccfd0a27f839889088ad838e1e806fd4fa54fd8bdef1595', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-056';
